{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Ephraim</b> — In His saying, 'Ephraim, what more have I?' — I have no need for them. I will answer him to give him all his desire, in the manner of 'and silver answers all' (Ecclesiastes 10:19)." "<b>and I will look upon him</b> — to set My eye for good upon him, until 'I will look upon him' is found to mean he will be like a flourishing cypress. And do not be afraid, for the cypress has no fruit, since 'your fruit is found from Me' (Hosea 14:8)."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:15.088748489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}